		"notes": "\n\t<p><i>Trout-faced sea-hag wearing seal-skin garb. Long, greasy black hair, cloying body odor. Transforms mortals into fish- scaled servants and mates.</i></p>\n\t<p></p>\n\t<p><strong>AC</strong> 12 (leather), <strong>HP</strong> 20, <strong>ATK</strong> 2 claw +4 (1d6 + grab) or 2 javelin (close/far) +4 (1d4), <strong>MV</strong> near (swim), <strong>S</strong> +3, <strong>D</strong> +1, <strong>C</strong> +2, <strong>I</strong> +1, <strong>W</strong> +1, <strong>Ch</strong> +1, <strong>AL</strong> <strong>C</strong>, <strong>LV</strong> 4</p><p></p>\n\t<p><strong>Grab</strong>. STR 15+ or held. STR 15+ on turn to break free.</p><p></p><p><strong>Scaly Curse</strong>. If target is grabbed or willing, CON 15+ each round or transformed into grindylow over 1d4 rounds. Slaying the qallupilluk stops the curse.</p><p></p>\n\t<p><i>Shadowfinder Complete Bestiary</i></p>",
